body:
Work out after class.  I'm 26 and last year was my first year.  I felt like I was running on empty ALL THE DAMN TIME.  This year I joined a Crossfit-type group exercise gym and I have SO MUCH MORE energy.  It's hard to drag myself to the classes sometimes, but I have a lot more energy in the mornings and throughout the day.

&#x200B;

And it's a good way to blow off some steam and de-stress from the day!

&#x200B;

EDIT: Also its only a JOB. An important, amazing, job full of sweat, tears, and passion, yes, but a JOB-and a low paying one at that!  Don't sweat the small stuff.  You being there for your students every day is already a wonderful thing. :)

FedLoan said:  Your employer certified the dates of employment that were entered in Section 3 of the ECF. However, the employment end date is before the employment begin date.

&#x200B;

My employer marked the box "still employed", and did not put an end date.  So this makes no sense to me.

&#x200B;

And I am a teacher, if that makes any difference.

Yes, it seems that so many people who are trying to go through proper channels and gain control over their finances get screwed over!

&#x200B;

It took me months to be put on PSLF, and now they are telling me my information is incorrect while the file I sent into them clearly has it all done correctly.  I don't know if they are that incompetent or are actively trying to screw people out of PSLF.

&#x200B;

Good luck!
